{% from "_macros.j2" import source, soon %}
{{ front }}

# Compliance card

At each stage gate ({{ stages | join(", ") | lower if stages else "data collection, model training and release" }}), the responsible developer records the status of each parameter together with a justification and evidence.

{{ source([S.card.link(page), S.compliance.link(page), S.metadata.link(page)]) }}

!!! note "Nothing leaves your browser"
    The form is not sent or stored anywhere. Download the card and submit it yourself (see [How to submit](#how-to-submit)).

{% set params = schema.properties.parameters.properties %}
{% if schema["x-status"] == "ok" %}
<div class="px-tool px-card" data-px-card data-version="{{ extra.version }}">
<script type="application/json" data-px-data>{{ schema | json }}</script>
<form class="px-card__form" onsubmit="return false">
<fieldset class="px-card__item">
<legend>What is this card for?</legend>
<label>Name of the dataset, model or service <input name="item.name" required></label>
<label>Type <select name="item.type"><option>Dataset</option><option>Model</option><option>Service</option></select></label>
<label>Version <input name="item.version"></label>
<label>Submitted by <input name="item.submitted_by"></label>
<label>Date <input type="date" name="item.date"></label>
<label>Stage gate <select name="stage" data-stage-select>{% for st in schema["x-stages"] %}<option value="{{ st | e }}">{{ st | e }}</option>{% endfor %}</select></label>
</fieldset>
{% for st, ids in schema["x-stages"].items() %}
<section class="px-card__stage" data-stage="{{ st | e }}" aria-label="Parameters: {{ st | e }}">
{% for pid in ids %}{% set p = params[pid] %}
<fieldset class="px-card__param">
<legend>{{ p.title | e }}</legend>
{% if p.get("description") %}<p class="px-card__desc">{{ p.description | e }}</p>{% endif %}
<label>Status {% if p.properties.status.get("enum") %}<select name="{{ pid }}.status"><option value="">–</option>{% for v in p.properties.status.enum %}<option>{{ v | e }}</option>{% endfor %}</select>{% else %}<input name="{{ pid }}.status">{% endif %}</label>
<label>Justification <textarea name="{{ pid }}.justification" rows="2"></textarea></label>
<label>Evidence <textarea name="{{ pid }}.evidence" rows="2" placeholder="Link, file name or report section"></textarea></label>
</fieldset>
{% endfor %}
</section>
{% endfor %}
</form>
<div class="px-toolbar">
<button type="button" class="md-button md-button--primary" data-action="json">Download JSON</button>
<button type="button" class="md-button" data-action="print">Print / save as PDF</button>
<button type="button" class="md-button" data-action="clear">Clear form</button>
</div>
</div>

The form follows [compliance_card.schema.json]({{ rel("data/compliance_card.schema.json") }}), generated from {{ S.card.link(page) }}.
{% else %}
{{ soon(S.card.link(page), "The parameter list for each stage gate. ") }}

Once it is in the guideline, this page becomes a form with the status, justification and evidence for every parameter, downloadable as JSON (for the metadata pipeline) and as a printable PDF.
{% endif %}

## How to submit

Send the downloaded card to the responsible AI reviewer before release, in either of two ways:

- **By email** to {{ extra.rai_contact }}, with the JSON file attached.
- **On GitHub**: open a [Compliance card submission]({{ repo }}/issues/new?template=compliance-card.yml) issue and attach the JSON file. Issues are public: do not attach personal or confidential data.

{{ source([S.compliance.link(page), S.governance.link(page)]) }}
